ine_handoff.py:316:    archive = facts[\"archive\"]\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:323:            \"role\": None, \"platform\": observed(archive.get(\"platform\")),\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:324:            \"transport\": {\"kind\": \"docker-archive\", \"artifact\": observed(archive[\"artifact\"]),\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:325:                          \"sha256\": observed(archive[\"sha256\"]), \"bytes\": observed(archive[\"bytes\"])},\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:326:            \"expected_image_config_id\": observed(archive.get(\"image_config_id\")),\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:328:            \"executable_sha256\": observed(archive.get(\"executables\")),\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:355:        handoff[\"provenance\"][identity] = archive.get(key, fact(None, \"missing\"))\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:489:    if at(handoff, \"release.transport.kind\") != \"docker-archive\":\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:490:        reject(\"release.transport.kind must be docker-archive\")\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:529:    actual_archive = None\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:540:                    actual_archive = (actual, nbytes)\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:542:                        inspection = observe_archive(target)\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:547:                                reject(identity + \": differs from re-observed archive\")\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:549:                        reject(f\"release.transport.artifact: archive observation failed: {exc}\")\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:561:                if actual_archive and (record.get(\"archive_sha256\"), record.get(\"archive_bytes\")) != actual_archive:\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:562:                    reject(\"build-record archive hash/bytes mismatch vs recomputed bytes\")\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:600:    for name in (\"build-record\", \"archive\", \"model-config\"):\ncc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py:615:            result = collect_facts(args.build_record, args.archive, args.model_config, args.gguf)\ncc/build_engine/README.md:21:To add a patch, save a unified Git diff to a file and add `--patch path/to/change.patch`. Source HEAD must resolve to `--commit`; tracked changes and untracked files cause rejection. The source checkout remains read-only: Git optional locks are disabled, a `git archive` snapshot is extracted under the output directory, and `git apply --check` runs there before `git apply`. Git discovery stops before the enclosing campaign repository. Binary patches supported by Git are accepted. Submodules are rejected. Git archive honors committed export attributes; ignored and untracked files and `.git` are omitted. Docker ignore files in the staged snapshot are emptied to prevent omission of tracked source. Temporary staging is removed after either result. Keep the supplied patch and original commit for rebuilding; patch bytes are identified by SHA256 but are not retained as a separate output artifact.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:25:## Engine variants and linkage\ncc/build_engine/README.md:39:  --linkage\ncc/build_engine/README.md:42:`--linkage` enables a final check after saving the image and collecting provenance. It runs one additional `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` against the built image's config ID, with a 60-second client timeout and no GPU. It discovers `/app/libggml-cuda.so` or a versioned `/app/libggml-cuda.so.*`, runs `ldd`, and selects `readelf -Ws` or, if unavailable, `nm -D`. A pass requires a dynamic `libcudart.so*` dependency and undefined imports of exactly `cudaMalloc`, `cudaFree`, and `cudaMemGetInfo` (including versioned symbols). Other CUDA API names and defined symbols do not satisfy the check. `ldd` showing `libcudart.so.12 => not found` still establishes a dynamic dependency; this check does not establish that runtime dependencies resolve on the GPU host.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:44:The record's `linkage` object contains `status` (`not_requested`, `passed`, `failed`, or `unavailable`), the discovered library, config ID, `libcudart_dynamic`, `undefined_imports`, each tool's return code/reason, and output paths. Missing tools, a missing library, nonzero tool exits, Docker failures, timeouts, and malformed probe output are `unavailable`; unavailable measurements are JSON null rather than false. Runtime images may lack both readelf and nm: the check explicitly records this rather than installing tools or silently claiming imports are absent.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:46:A failed or unavailable requested check sets top-level `failure_stage=\"linkage\"` and exits 1, while preserving the saved archive and other evidence. `--linkage-optional` enables the same check (even without `--linkage`) but permits a failed/unavailable result with overall success and exit 0; inspect `linkage.status` in that case. With neither flag, linkage is `not_requested`.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:48:The probe saves `linkage.raw.txt` (framed stdout), `linkage.stderr.txt` (Docker/probe stderr), `linkage.ldd.txt`, and `linkage.symbols.txt`. Tool stderr is merged into its corresponding raw tool output. On a Docker error or malformed probe, only the first two files may be available. This ELF check does not prove allocation interception, actual pool selection, or GPU execution; the orchestrator must verify `NO_VMM = 1` and allocation events under the budget shim.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:52:`build-record.json` uses schema version 2. Version 1 evidence remains untouched; this capability has no build-record reader. Schema 2 adds `cmake_defines`, `recipe_sha256`, and `linkage`; `cmake_flags` includes all built-in and extra definitions. It records status, failure stage/error, requested and resolved commit, Git tree ID and dirty status, patch SHA256 or null, tag/platform, recipe SHA256 and sizes, base references/digests, Docker and Buildx versions, CMake flags, Buildx metadata, image config ID/RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/Os, tool SHA256 values, saved archive SHA256/bytes, build duration and total duration. Fields remain null or empty when a failure occurs before collection. `build_wall_seconds` measures the Bake invocation, including export; `wall_seconds` covers the whole attempt.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:56:- `build.stdout` and `build.stderr`: full subprocess stdout/stderr, including compiler output and diagnostics on failure. Binary Git archive output is directed to staging rather than the logs.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:60:The CLI exits 0 only after all required evidence collection succeeds, otherwise nonzero; `--linkage-optional` permits a recorded linkage failure. Failures include source mismatch/dirty tree, unsupported submodules, malformed or inapplicable patch, unavailable Docker/base image, build/export failure, incorrect architecture, missing binaries, save failure, or malformed archive. A failure after building can leave the tagged local image and partial evidence; inspect `failure_stage` and retry in a fresh output directory. Invalid CLI arguments, an unwritable output path, or a nonempty output directory fail before a record can be created. Existing evidence is never overwritten. The CLI does not push, prune, mount the Docker socket in an image, or operate on unrelated containers. A short-lived `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` container hashes the tools and libraries without requesting a GPU. After resolving the tag once, saving uses the immutable Docker-reported ID. Before hashing or linkage, the archive inspector follows the OCI catalog and nested indexes to the linux/amd64 image manifest and config, skipping other platforms and attestations. It verifies the SHA256 of referenced JSON blobs and requires exactly one matching config. Classic Docker archives are supported by hashing the config bytes named in `manifest.json`. Hashing and optional linkage then use this config digest as the local `sha256:...` Docker image ID; local-only `repo@digest` references are not used. Buildx `containerimage.config.digest` is optional and is cross-checked against the archive when present. Index metadata is cross-checked when the archive retains the index. Missing, ambiguous, or inconsistent archive identities fail before runtime probes. The record keeps `Id`/`docker_reported_id`, `config_digest`, `manifest_digest`, `index_digest`, `index_manifests`, and `docker_id_in_archive_index` separate; an unavailable manifest or index digest is null. `index.json` is the archive catalog and is not assumed to be the original image index.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:62:Bake requests maximum provenance and saves metadata separately. This does not imply provenance survives image loading and `docker save`. The archive inspector checks `index.json` and reachable OCI manifests for actual in-toto SLSA provenance statements. A classic Docker archive without an OCI index records `retained: false`; an SBOM or an attestation annotation alone does not count. A save or inspection failure leaves provenance unconfirmed. No signature or attestation trust verification is performed.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:66:The CLI stages its recipes in `.campaign-recipe/` inside the archived source context. Bake receives digest-pinned base references, source and patch identity, extra targets, and extra definitions from the CLI. Prefer the CLI for validation and evidence collection; direct builds using the older `builds/llamacpp/` recipes do not support these variant options.\ncc/build_engine/README.md:77:Tests use temporary Git repositories and mocked Docker subprocesses. They cover patch rejection, successful patch isolation, successful record schema, build failure logs/metadata, dirty or mismatched source, archive/tool hashing, provenance versus SBOM, and refusing to overwrite evidence. They also cover define validation, variant recipe identity/build arguments/labels, schema 2, captured ELF linkage fixtures, shell tool selection, config-ID versus index-ID targeting, and fatal/optional linkage failures. The T-N2 regression uses the real containerd Buildx metadata fixture without config metadata, plus constructed content-addressed OCI index/manifest/config archives (with another platform and an attestation). It checks config metadata mismatches, missing or corrupt configs, ambiguous configs, and index metadata mismatches before any runtime probe. They use no network, GPU, or real engine build.\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:21:def classic_archive():\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:26:def oci_archive():\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:53:def linkage_output(ldd=None, symbols=None, tool=\"readelf\", ldd_rc=0, symbols_rc=0):\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:57:            + (symbols if symbols is not None else (FIXTURES / \"readelf.txt\").read_text())\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:85:    with tarfile.open(path, \"w\") as archive:\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:90:            archive.addfile(member, io.BytesIO(data))\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:168:                result = state.get(\"linkage_output\", linkage_output())\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:169:                code = state.get(\"linkage_code\", 0)\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:171:                if state.get(\"linkage_timeout\"):\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:179:            make_tar(command[command.index(\"--output\") + 1], state.get(\"archive\", classic_archive()))\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:206:    assert result[\"linkage\"] == {\"status\": \"not_requested\"}\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:213:    assert result[\"archive\"][\"sha256\"] == engine.file_digest(Path(args.out) / result[\"archive\"][\"path\"])[\"sha256\"]\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:214:    assert result[\"archive\"][\"bytes\"] > 0\ncc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py:288:    assert engine.archive_provenance(path)[\"retained