{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_14","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '50,147p' cc/build_engine/build_engine.py && sed -n '25,52p' cc/build_engine/README.md && git diff --stat -- cc/build_engine && ls -lh builds/results/shot-2/engine-image.docker.tar\"","aggregated_output":"    recipes = {name: file_digest(RECIPES / name)\n               for name in (\"Dockerfile\", \"docker-bake.hcl\")}\n    inputs = {\"recipes\": recipes, \"cmake_defines\": defines,\n              \"cmake_flags\": CMAKE_FLAGS, \"extra_targets\": list(extra_targets)}\n    digest = hashlib.sha256(json.dumps(inputs, sort_keys=True, separators=(\",\", \":\")).encode()).hexdigest()\n    return recipes, digest\n\n\nLINKAGE_SYMBOLS = (\"cudaMalloc\", \"cudaFree\", \"cudaMemGetInfo\")\nLINKAGE_SCRIPT = r'''\nlibrary=\"\"\nfor candidate in /app/libggml-cuda.so /app/libggml-cuda.so.*; do\n    if [ -f \"$candidate\" ]; then library=\"$candidate\"; break; fi\ndone\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_LIBRARY__%s\\n' \"$library\"\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_LDD_BEGIN__\\n'\nif [ -z \"$library\" ]; then\n    echo 'CUDA backend library not found in /app'; ldd_rc=125\nelif command -v ldd >/dev/null 2>&1; then\n    ldd \"$library\" 2>&1; ldd_rc=$?\nelse\n    echo 'ldd unavailable in runtime image'; ldd_rc=127\nfi\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_LDD_END__%s\\n' \"$ldd_rc\"\n# Symbols and DT_NEEDED are inspected from the saved archive on the host.\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_BEGIN__host\\n'\nprintf '__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_END__0\\n'\n'''\n\n\ndef parse_linkage(ldd_text, symbols_text, *, symbol_tool=\"readelf\",\n                  ldd_returncode=0, symbols_returncode=0):\n    dynamic = None if ldd_returncode else bool(re.search(r\"\\blibcudart\\.so(?:\\.[\\w.]+)?\\b\", ldd_text))\n    imports = {name: None for name in LINKAGE_SYMBOLS}\n    if not symbols_returncode and symbol_tool in (\"readelf\", \"nm\"):\n        for name in imports:\n            if symbol_tool == \"readelf\":\n                pattern = r\"\\bUND\\s+\" + name + r\"(?:@\\S+)?(?:\\s|$)\"\n            else:\n                pattern = r\"^\\s*(?:[0-9a-fA-F]+\\s+)?[Uwv]\\s+\" + name + r\"(?:@\\S+)?(?:\\s|$)\"\n            imports[name] = bool(re.search(pattern, symbols_text, re.MULTILINE))\n    unavailable = bool(ldd_returncode or symbols_returncode or symbol_tool not in (\"readelf\", \"nm\"))\n    passed = dynamic is True and all(value is True for value in imports.values())\n    return {\"status\": \"unavailable\" if unavailable else \"passed\" if passed else \"failed\",\n            \"libcudart_dynamic\": dynamic, \"undefined_imports\": imports,\n            \"ldd\": {\"returncode\": ldd_returncode,\n                    \"reason\": ldd_text.strip() if ldd_returncode else None},\n            \"symbols\": {\"tool\": symbol_tool, \"returncode\": symbols_returncode,\n                        \"reason\": symbols_text.strip() if symbols_returncode or symbol_tool == \"unavailable\" else None}}\n\n\ndef collect_linkage(run, out, image_id, archive):\n    result = {\"status\": \"unavailable\", \"image_config_id\": image_id,\n              \"libcudart_dynamic\": None, \"undefined_imports\": dict.fromkeys(LINKAGE_SYMBOLS),\n              \"raw_output\": \"linkage.raw.txt\", \"stderr_output\": \"linkage.stderr.txt\"}\n    try:\n        run([\"docker\", \"run\", \"--rm\", \"--network=none\", \"--read-only\",\n             \"--entrypoint\", \"/bin/sh\", image_id, \"-c\", LINKAGE_SCRIPT],\n            stdout_path=out / \"linkage.raw.txt\", stderr_path=out / \"linkage.stderr.txt\", timeout=60)\n        raw = (out / \"linkage.raw.txt\").read_text()\n        match = re.fullmatch(r\"__CAMPAIGN_LIBRARY__([^\\n]*)\\n__CAMPAIGN_LDD_BEGIN__\\n(.*?)\"\n                             r\"__CAMPAIGN_LDD_END__(\\d+)\\n__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_BEGIN__(\\w+)\\n(.*?)\"\n                             r\"__CAMPAIGN_SYMBOLS_END__(\\d+)\\n\", raw, re.DOTALL)\n        if not match:\n            raise ValueError(\"Malformed linkage probe output; see linkage.raw.txt and linkage.stderr.txt\")\n        library, ldd, ldd_rc, tool, symbols, symbols_rc = match.groups()\n        (out / \"linkage.ldd.txt\").write_text(ldd)\n        (out / \"linkage.symbols.txt\").write_text(symbols)\n        result.update(parse_linkage(ldd, symbols, symbol_tool=tool,\n                                   ldd_returncode=int(ldd_rc), symbols_returncode=int(symbols_rc)))\n        result.update(library=library or None, ldd_output=\"linkage.ldd.txt\",\n                      symbols_output=\"linkage.symbols.txt\")\n    except Exception as exc:\n        result.update(status=\"unavailable\", reason=str(exc))\n    # Host ELF evidence determines status even when the in-image ldd probe fails.\n    # Retain its diagnostics independently; ldd cannot establish DT_NEEDED itself.\n    result[\"ldd_libcudart_dynamic\"] = result.get(\"libcudart_dynamic\")\n    host = collect_host_linkage(archive, temp_parent=out)\n    if \"reason\" in result:\n        result[\"ldd_probe_reason\"] = result.pop(\"reason\")\n    result.update(host)\n    (out / \"linkage.symbols.txt\").write_text(json.dumps(host, indent=2, sort_keys=True) + \"\\n\")\n    result[\"symbols_output\"] = \"linkage.symbols.txt\"\n    return result\n\n\ndef file_digest(path):\n    digest = hashlib.sha256()\n    size = 0\n    with Path(path).open(\"rb\") as stream:\n        for chunk in iter(lambda: stream.read(1024 * 1024), b\"\"):\n            digest.update(chunk)\n            size += len(chunk)\n    return {\"sha256\": digest.hexdigest(), \"bytes\": size}\n\n\ndef archive_identities(path):\n    \"\"\"Read the linux/amd64 config through OCI indexes or a classic Docker manifest.\n## Engine variants and linkage\n\nUse repeatable `--cmake-define KEY=VALUE` options. Keys must match `^[A-Z0-9_]+$`; values must be nonempty and contain only ASCII letters, digits, or `_./:+,@%=-`. Whitespace, shell metacharacters, empty values, duplicate keys (even with identical values), and all built-in keys are rejected before output creation. This also reserves the built-in compiler-launcher and executable-linker flags. Definitions are sorted by key, passed as the `CMAKE_DEFINES` build argument as space-separated `-DKEY=VALUE` words, and stored in the runtime image label `campaign.cmake.defines` in that same format. The CLI overwrites inherited `CMAKE_DEFINES` environment values.\n\n`recipes` records the SHA256 and size of each recipe file. `recipe_sha256` hashes canonical JSON (sorted keys, compact separators) containing those file identities, all built-in flags, the definitions, and extra targets. Definition values therefore change recipe identity even when recipe bytes are unchanged; reordering definitions does not.\n\nFor the GPU budget shim, build with VMM disabled at compile time. From the campaign root, with a clean source checkout at the shown commit and local base images available:\n\n```bash\npython3 cc/build_engine/build_engine.py \\\n  --source ref/llama.cpp --commit 31288c9c66e59377f7788d920678a565bb89dd37 \\\n  --tag campaign/llamacpp:no-vmm \\\n  --out artifacts/codexN/no-vmm-build \\\n  --cmake-define GGML_CUDA_NO_VMM=ON \\\n  --linkage\n```\n\n`--linkage` enables a final check after saving the image and collecting provenance. It runs one additional `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh` against the built image's config ID, with a 60-second client timeout and no GPU. It discovers `/app/libggml-cuda.so` or a versioned `/app/libggml-cuda.so.*`, runs `ldd`, and selects `readelf -Ws` or, if unavailable, `nm -D`. A pass requires a dynamic `libcudart.so*` dependency and undefined imports of exactly `cudaMalloc`, `cudaFree`, and `cudaMemGetInfo` (including versioned symbols). Other CUDA API names and defined symbols do not satisfy the check. `ldd` showing `libcudart.so.12 => not found` still establishes a dynamic dependency; this check does not establish that runtime dependencies resolve on the GPU host.\n\nThe record's `linkage` object contains `status` (`not_requested`, `passed`, `failed`, or `unavailable`), the discovered library, config ID, `libcudart_dynamic`, `undefined_imports`, each tool's return code/reason, and output paths. Missing tools, a missing library, nonzero tool exits, Docker failures, timeouts, and malformed probe output are `unavailable`; unavailable measurements are JSON null rather than false. Runtime images may lack both readelf and nm: the check explicitly records this rather than installing tools or silently claiming imports are absent.\n\nA failed or unavailable requested check sets top-level `failure_stage=\"linkage\"` and exits 1, while preserving the saved archive and other evidence. `--linkage-optional` enables the same check (even without `--linkage`) but permits a failed/unavailable result with overall success and exit 0; inspect `linkage.status` in that case. With neither flag, linkage is `not_requested`.\n\nThe probe saves `linkage.raw.txt` (framed stdout), `linkage.stderr.txt` (Docker/probe stderr), `linkage.ldd.txt`, and `linkage.symbols.txt`. Tool stderr is merged into its corresponding raw tool output. On a Docker error or malformed probe, only the first two files may be available. This ELF check does not prove allocation interception, actual pool selection, or GPU execution; the orchestrator must verify `NO_VMM = 1` and allocation events under the budget shim.\n\n## Outputs and failure handling\n\n`build-record.json` uses schema version 2. Version 1 evidence remains untouched; this capability has no build-record reader. Schema 2 adds `cmake_defines`, `recipe_sha256`, and `linkage`; `cmake_flags` includes all built-in and extra definitions. It records status, failure stage/error, requested and resolved commit, Git tree ID and dirty status, patch SHA256 or null, tag/platform, recipe SHA256 and sizes, base references/digests, Docker and Buildx versions, CMake flags, Buildx metadata, image config ID/RepoDigests/Created/Architecture/Os, tool SHA256 values, saved archive SHA256/bytes, build duration and total duration. Fields remain null or empty when a failure occurs before collection. `build_wall_seconds` measures the Bake invocation, including export; `wall_seconds` covers the whole attempt.\n campaign/cc/build_engine/build_engine.py      | 31 +++++++++---------\n campaign/cc/build_engine/test_build_engine.py | 47 +++++++++++++++------------\n 2 files changed, 42 insertions(+), 36 deletions(-)\n-rw------- 1 muk muk 2.1G Nov  9 22:30 builds/results/shot-2/engine-image.docker.tar\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_15","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\np='cc/build_engine/README.md'\ns=open(p).read()\na=s.index('\"'`--linkage` enables a final check'\"')\nb=s.index('\\\\nA failed or unavailable',a)\ns=s[:a]+'''\"'`--linkage` enables a final check after saving the image and collecting provenance. The saved OCI or classic Docker archive supplies the symbol evidence: layer contents are streamed with blob and rootfs digest checks, whiteouts are merged, and `/app/libggml-cuda.so` (or a versioned variant) is resolved through its link chain. Only the resolved library is copied into a temporary directory, which is removed after inspection. This follows the streaming/whiteout approach in `cc/engine_handoff/engine_handoff.py`, without extracting the image filesystem.\n\nA pure Python ELF reader (`symbols.tool=\"python-elf\"`, `symbols.location=\"host\"`) reads dynamic symbols and `DT_NEEDED`; neither the host nor runtime image needs readelf or nm. It supports ELF32/64 and both byte orders. ELF files without usable dynamic section headers are explicitly unavailable. A pass requires a found library, a `libcudart.so` or `libcudart.so.*` entry in `DT_NEEDED`, and an undefined `cudaMalloc` import. The record also reports undefined `cudaFree`, `cudaMallocAsync`, `cudaFreeAsync`, `cudaMemGetInfo`, and `cuMemCreate` imports; their absence does not fail the check. Defined symbols and lookalike names do not count.\n\nThe existing in-image `ldd` probe runs with `docker run --rm --network=none --read-only --entrypoint /bin/sh`, the immutable local `run_ref`, a 60-second client timeout, and no GPU. Its output, return code, and `ldd_libcudart_dynamic` remain separate evidence. Missing runtime tools, failed Docker probes, timeouts, or malformed probe output are recorded without changing the host ELF result. This check does not establish that runtime dependencies resolve on the GPU host.\n\nThe record'\"'s \"'`linkage` object 